message: "If you use or discuss this method, please cite this technical note."
title: "Atomic Semantic Firewall for System One Models: Exhaustive Atomic Rule-State Verification for High-Recall Semantic Quality Control"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Zhang"
    given-names: "Liang"
date-released: "2026-09-23"
version: "0.1"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
keywords:
  - System One Models
  - semantic verification
  - atomic rules
  - semantic firewall
  - high-recall quality assurance
  - exhaustive verification
abstract: >-
  Atomic Semantic Firewall is an architecture for compiling large natural-language
  knowledge assets into atomic semantic constraints and verifying bounded local
  state windows against large or exhaustive rule sets using high-throughput
  System One Models, with anomalies escalated to System Two reasoning.
